            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0530" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 29/364: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-19T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:07 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1535. For attention of Davis.</p>
                <p>Communicated orally to Eyre Crowe of the Foreign Office substance of Boyden’s
                    B–239 of September 10 and your B–134 of October <pb facs="0531" n="441"
                        xml:id="pg441"/> 6 to Boyden. Our position appears understood and
                    appreciated as it was quite frankly stated that without approval of British and
                    ourselves nothing definite could be done and matter seems now to have narrowed
                    down to constitution of delegation to preliminary conference. Have informed
                    Boyden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
